selftext:
Hi everyone,

Meet **Core Echo**, a pixel art mining game you can play right in your browser, on phone or desktop.

The loop is simple: pilot a drill, dig deeper, head back up to sell your ores, upgrade your machine, then go even deeper. Over time the game opens up:

* a growing village (Forge, Workbench, Smelter, Lab…) with buildings you can place freely;
* crafting (alloys, drill parts, items, modules);
* a crew of miners you send on missions;
* other planets to explore, each with its own resources;
* and a story to piece together: a mysterious Signal calling you from the depths.

The twist: **I’m not a developer. The whole game was vibe coded.** I describe what I want, an AI (Claude) writes the code, and I test and iterate. The art was generated, then touched up.

It’s free, no ads, and you can add it to your home screen to play offline.

👉 **\[link to the game in comment\]**

I’d love honest feedback to make it better, especially on:

* the first few minutes: is it clear what to do?
* pacing: when does it get repetitive or too slow?
* readability on mobile (text, buttons, controls);
* bugs or slowdowns;
* what made you want to keep playing, or to stop.

Thanks to anyone who gives it a try!
